---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ArticleSchema from '../../components/ArticleSchema.astro';
import TldrBox from '../../components/TldrBox.astro';
import FaqSection from '../../components/FaqSection.astro';
import { site, description, pageTitle } from '../../content';
import { appBySlug } from '../../data/apps';

const a = appBySlug('klaviyo')!;
const b = appBySlug('yotpo-email-sms')!;
const path = '/compare/klaviyo-vs-yotpo-email-sms';
const title = pageTitle(site, 'compare/klaviyo-vs-yotpo-email-sms');
const desc = description(site, 'compare/klaviyo-vs-yotpo-email-sms');
const faqs = [
  {
    "question": "Can I choose Yotpo Email & SMS today?",
    "answer": "No. Yotpo announced full deprecation for December 31, 2025; evaluate a current sender and reconcile retained records."
  },
  {
    "question": "Is Klaviyo an official Yotpo migration partner?",
    "answer": "The cited Yotpo announcement names Omnisend and Attentive. Evaluate Klaviyo independently rather than implying partner status."
  },
  {
    "question": "Which Klaviyo events need separate checks?",
    "answer": "Added to Cart and Checkout Started represent different stages. Verify their metric sources, message payloads and purchase exclusions."
  },
  {
    "question": "What does the $253 model show?",
    "answer": "At 34% gross margin, full-price gross profit is $86.02. A 14% code leaves $50.60 with fixed product cost, a $35.42 reduction before other variable costs."
  }
];
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={desc} site={site} path={path}>
  <ArticleSchema title={title} description={desc} siteName={site.name} domain={site.domain} path={path} />
  <section class="py-14 md:py-20"><div class="container">
    <a href="/compare" class="link text-sm font-bold">← Comparisons</a>
    <h1 class="hero-title mt-6">Klaviyo as a replacement for retired Yotpo Email & SMS</h1>
    <p class="mt-7 max-w-3xl text-xl leading-9 text-[#4a2d17]">This is a replacement and data-reconciliation decision. Yotpo Email & SMS is no longer a current sender purchase option.</p>
    <TldrBox picks={[{ label: "Evaluate", tool: a.name, reason: "Evaluate Klaviyo against your Shopify events" },{ label: "Context", tool: b.name, reason: "Historical sender; retirement changes the decision" }]} />
    <div class="mt-12 card overflow-x-auto"><table class="data-table"><thead><tr><th>Decision</th><th>{a.name}</th><th>{b.name}</th></tr></thead><tbody>
      <tr><td>Status</td><td>Evaluate Klaviyo against your Shopify events</td><td>Historical sender; retirement changes the decision</td></tr>
      <tr><td>First task</td><td>Map Added to Cart and Checkout Started separately</td><td>Locate retained consent and suppression records</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Cutover owner</td><td>Own new flow eligibility and purchase exits</td><td>Reconcile legacy queues and unresolved opt-outs</td></tr>
    </tbody></table></div>
    <article class="prose-shopify mt-14 max-w-4xl">
      <h2>Yotpo retirement changes the shortlist</h2>
      <p>Yotpo announced full deprecation of Email and SMS for December 31, 2025. Its Reviews and Loyalty products are separate from the retired sender. A store retaining those products still needs to evaluate a current sending platform. Yotpo named Omnisend and Attentive as migration partners; this is not evidence that Klaviyo is an official migration partner or a universal replacement winner.</p>
      <h2>Rebuild event meaning before importing audiences</h2>
      <p>In Klaviyo, a Shopify Checkout Started flow addresses shoppers who reached checkout. Added to Cart addresses an earlier stage and requires its own event and content checks. Inspect the actual metric source in a test profile, especially if an older custom tracking implementation exists. Do not connect both legacy and replacement metrics to live flows without testing duplicate entry.</p>
      <h2>Reconcile available records, not imagined dashboard access</h2>
      <p>Start from exports already retained, Shopify orders and records the business can actually access. Ask the vendor about missing records; do not assume the retired dashboard still supports export. Map email and SMS permission separately, including purpose, source and timestamp where available. Preserve opt-outs and unresolved suppression records rather than treating imported profiles as permission to send.</p>
      <h2>Prove the replacement with distinct shopper paths</h2>
      <p>Use an identified cart that never starts checkout, a cart that progresses to checkout, and a purchase while a reminder waits. Verify trigger, product payload, checkout link and the Placed Order exclusion in each path. Test a returning purchaser and an email-only subscriber separately. A missing event is an integration defect to resolve, not a reason to send a broader campaign.</p>
      <h2>Retain the $253 margin decision</h2>
      <p>Illustrative fixed-cost model: a $253 cart at 34% gross margin has $166.98 product cost and $86.02 gross profit at full price. A 14% code reduces revenue to $217.58 and gross profit to $50.60, losing $35.42 before messaging, shipping, taxes and returns. This is arithmetic, not a supplier result. Start with help for a subscription toggle or financing question rather than assuming a discount solves it.</p>
      <h2>Control cutover and remaining product integrations</h2>
      <p>Name one owner for the new send queue. Disable competing live recovery sends before enabling the replacement; compare eligibility without sending twice. Recheck current purchase, stock, permission and suppression before release. Deduplicate replayed events using stable source identifiers. Verify any Reviews or Loyalty fields independently so a missing reward balance cannot silently select the wrong incentive.</p>
      <h2>Documentation checked November 25, 2026</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><a href="https://www.yotpo.com/blog/email-sms-migration-partners/">Yotpo retirement announcement</a></li>
        <li><a href="https://help.klaviyo.com/hc/en-us/articles/35510464880027">Klaviyo Added to Cart flow</a></li>
        <li><a href="https://help.klaviyo.com/hc/en-us/articles/115005080447">Klaviyo Shopify data reference</a></li>
      </ul>
    </article>
    <FaqSection faqs={faqs} title={`${a.name} vs ${b.name} FAQ`} />
  </div></section>
</BaseLayout>
